Hi Team,

As I have recently been assigned this application and have not worked on it previously, I would like to propose a phased testing approach for the upcoming releases.

The initial focus should be on understanding the application and establishing a reliable functional testing baseline before moving into automation.

Immediate / Short-Term Activities

Attend basic KT sessions to understand the application, major business flows, integrations, and critical functionalities.
Get the required application, environment, database, API, and other relevant accesses.
Review any available existing test cases, previous release documents, known issues, and production defects.
Identify the most critical business flows and prepare a basic smoke test suite that can be executed quickly for every build/release.
Start developing a structured regression test suite covering the main end-to-end business scenarios.
Identify the required test data and any dependencies on other systems or teams.
Review previous defects to understand historically high-risk areas of the application.

These activities can give us relatively quick coverage and also help build a better understanding of the system.

Medium-Term Activities

Once the regression suite is reasonably mature, we can review the test cases to identify good candidates for automation.

The automation assessment should consider:

Frequently executed regression scenarios
Stable application functionality
Repetitive and time-consuming manual tests
Critical business scenarios
Data-driven scenarios
API or backend validations where applicable

Based on this assessment, we can prioritize the automation candidates instead of trying to automate the complete regression suite.

Long-Term Activities

After identifying the right automation candidates, we can define a proper automation roadmap, including:

Selection or evaluation of the automation framework/tools
Development of reusable automation components
Automation of prioritized regression scenarios
Integration of automated tests with the CI/CD pipeline, where possible
Automated test execution and reporting
Test-data management
Regular maintenance of regression and automation suites
Gradual increase of automated regression coverage based on business value and release risk

I believe the first practical milestone should be to establish the KT + Smoke Suite + Regression Test Suite. Once we have that baseline, we will be in a much better position to decide what should be automated and how much effort will be required.

This approach should allow us to deliver some immediate testing value while building a sustainable testing and automation strategy for future releases.

Please let me know if you have any suggestions or if there are any additional areas you would like me to include in this plan.

